-- title:
--   Theorem 3.2 — Lovász Local Lemma, symmetric version
-- statement:
--   Let $A_1,\dots,A_n$ be events in a probability space and $p\in[0,1)$ with $\mathbb P(A_i)\le p$ for all $i$. Suppose each $A_i$ is mutually independent of a set of all but at most $d_{\mathrm{LLL}}$ of the other events. If $4pd_{\mathrm{LLL}}\le 1$, then
--   $$\mathbb P\Big(\bigcap_i A_i^{\mathrm c}\Big)>0.$$
--
--   The symmetric Local Lemma glues the bad events of one nibble step in Lemma 4.7.
--
--   **Formalization Note** Mutual independence of $A_i$ from a set of events is independence from the σ-algebra they generate.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: A_i mutually independent of a set of events → Indep of generateFrom {A i} and generateFrom (A '' S i), with the events measurable; reason: the standard meaning of mutual independence
-- source:
--   Dhawan, Methuku, Vo, List Coloring Uncrowded Hypergraphs at the Shattering Threshold, STOC 2027 submission (manuscript sha256 2e7243ce…), Theorem 3.2, p.14

import Mathlib

open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory

namespace UncrowdedColoring

/-- **Theorem 3.2 (Lovász Local Lemma, symmetric version)**, p.14.

Dhawan, Methuku, Vo, *List Coloring Uncrowded Hypergraphs at the Shattering Threshold*, STOC 2027
submission (manuscript sha256 2e7243ce…), Theorem 3.2, p.14.

**Formalization Note.** A general probability space with measurable events. "`A_i` is mutually
independent of a set of events" is independence of `A_i` from the σ-algebra generated by that set. `S i`
is that set; at most `dLLL` of the other events lie outside it. `dLLL = 0` and `p = 0` are allowed. -/
theorem theorem_3_2 {Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] (μ : Measure Ω) [IsProbabilityMeasure μ]
    (n : ℕ) (A : Fin n → Set Ω) (hA : ∀ i, MeasurableSet (A i))
    (p : ℝ) (hp₀ : 0 ≤ p) (hp₁ : p < 1) (hpA : ∀ i, μ.real (A i) ≤ p)
    (dLLL : ℕ) (S : Fin n → Finset (Fin n)) (hS : ∀ i, i ∉ S i)
    (hcard : ∀ i, ((Finset.univ.erase i) \ S i).card ≤ dLLL)
    (hind : ∀ i, Indep (MeasurableSpace.generateFrom {A i})
      (MeasurableSpace.generateFrom (A '' (S i : Set (Fin n)))) μ)
    (h4 : 4 * p * (dLLL : ℝ) ≤ 1) :
    0 < μ (⋂ i, (A i)ᶜ) := by sorry

end UncrowdedColoring
